WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.173 --> 00:00:17.994
Jack stood with Hulk and Laura on the deck of the pool.

2
00:00:18.695 --> 00:00:22.276
The Sharks' swim meet against the Pacific Piranhas was about to start.

3
00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:27.418
Mrs. Wilson walked over to Hulk and spread her arms wide.

4
00:00:27.438 --> 00:00:31.900
"One last hug for my precious little Tommy."

5
00:00:33.164 --> 00:00:36.145
"You're the precious one, Grammy," Hulk said as they hugged.

6
00:00:37.505 --> 00:00:40.306
"You're the best grandmother in the whole wide world."

7
00:00:40.326 --> 00:00:45.587
"And you're the best grandson there ever was," Mrs.

8
00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:46.468
Wilson cooed.

9
00:00:47.148 --> 00:00:49.929
Laura nudged Jack and mimed throwing up.

10
00:00:52.069 --> 00:00:52.830
Jack laughed.

11
00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:55.770
Listening to Mrs.

12
00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:00.032
Wilson and Hulk was almost as nauseating as listening to the Long-Hair Boys.

13
00:01:01.192 --> 00:01:03.577
Still, he liked this version of Mrs.

14
00:01:03.617 --> 00:01:05.277
Wilson better than the cranky one.

15
00:01:06.038 --> 00:01:08.979
He wondered if her near-death experience had transformed her.

16
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.400
Suddenly Mrs.

17
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.761
Wilson spun toward Jack and jabbed her finger into his chest.

18
00:01:14.781 --> 00:01:19.943
"My little Tommy said you're swimming breaststroke on his relay team.

19
00:01:20.363 --> 00:01:23.225
You'd better not ruin his race, young man."

20
00:01:23.245 --> 00:01:25.225
"Yes, ma'am!"

21
00:01:25.746 --> 00:01:26.306
Jack said.

22
00:01:27.006 --> 00:01:27.947
Obviously, Mrs.

23
00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:31.208
Wilson's near-death experience hadn't changed her at all.

24
00:01:32.552 --> 00:01:40.195
As she made her way to the chairs alongside the pool, Jack muttered to Laura, "I'm still waiting

25
00:01:40.235 --> 00:01:43.217
to be thanked for that little favor—saving her life."

26
00:01:44.357 --> 00:01:45.058
Laura giggled.

27
00:01:45.078 --> 00:01:47.439
"Good luck with that," she said.

28
00:01:47.459 --> 00:01:49.520
"She'd rather yell at you."

29
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.481
Just then the announcer lifted his megaphone.

30
00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:59.384
"The boys' two-hundred-meter medley relay will start in two minutes."

31
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.581
Coach Shin patted Jack's back.

32
00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:06.342
"We need to win this," he said sternly.

33
00:02:08.042 --> 00:02:08.722
Jack shivered.

34
00:02:09.282 --> 00:02:10.163
He felt nervous.

35
00:02:11.243 --> 00:02:17.645
It would be horrible to perform poorly, especially after he and Hulk and Laura had spent so much

36
00:02:17.785 --> 00:02:20.445
effort convincing their coach to let him participate.

37
00:02:22.026 --> 00:02:25.247
But the kids on the Pacific Piranhas team were very good swimmers.

38
00:02:25.987 --> 00:02:27.967
It was going to be a challenging race.

39
00:02:29.168 --> 00:02:33.081
The starter blew a whistle, signaling the backstroke swimmers to get ready.

40
00:02:33.101 --> 00:02:39.883
"Good luck," Jack told his teammate Sebastian as Sebastian got into the water.

41
00:02:39.903 --> 00:02:42.843
"Good luck to you too.

42
00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:46.304
The four of us have to win this thing," Sebastian said.

43
00:02:46.324 --> 00:02:48.385
"But no pressure, right?"

44
00:02:48.685 --> 00:02:49.305
Jack joked.

45
00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:53.786
Sebastian frowned, obviously feeling a whole lot of pressure.

46
00:02:54.727 --> 00:02:57.547
The starter checked to make sure everyone was in position.

47
00:02:58.388 --> 00:03:02.602
Then a horn sounded, and the six backstroke specialists were off.

48
00:03:07.365 --> 00:03:10.368
Sebastian started quickly but lost steam.

49
00:03:11.188 --> 00:03:14.811
As he approached the far end of the pool, he was in the middle of the pack.

50
00:03:15.611 --> 00:03:17.032
He had paced himself poorly.

51
00:03:18.453 --> 00:03:20.755
At the turn Sebastian lost more time.

52
00:03:22.576 --> 00:03:27.240
Now he was stroking back toward Jack, but he was falling farther and farther behind.

53
00:03:30.816 --> 00:03:36.341
Jack's relay team would lose for sure unless Jack was one of the fastest breaststrokers in the pool.

54
00:03:36.862 --> 00:03:37.742
But Jack wasn't.

55
00:03:38.964 --> 00:03:42.827
He'd been a standout in Oklahoma, but he wasn't one here in California.

56
00:03:43.608 --> 00:03:47.171
He was going to lose his— "Focus, Jack!"

57
00:03:47.651 --> 00:03:48.352
he heard Mrs.

58
00:03:48.412 --> 00:03:50.734
Wilson shout, snapping him to attention.

59
00:03:51.435 --> 00:03:56.880
"Streamline the dive, cup your hands, and bring your head down far enough!"

60
00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:04.189
By the time Sebastian touched the wall and finished his fifty meters, Jack was totally focused.

61
00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:10.594
He dived into the water fast, making sure to keep his head down and his legs together.

62
00:04:12.796 --> 00:04:15.818
Yes! His dive was perfectly streamlined.

63
00:04:17.559 --> 00:04:20.662
Once Jack was in the water, he kept his body streamlined.

64
00:04:21.362 --> 00:04:24.165
He made sure his head wasn't too high, as Mrs.

65
00:04:24.245 --> 00:04:25.546
Wilson had kept telling him.

66
00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:31.009
His arms and legs were extended, with his fingers pointed ahead and his toes behind him.

67
00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:33.410
He swept out his arms.

68
00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:38.111
His head and chest exploded out of the water as he propelled his body forward.

69
00:04:41.172 --> 00:04:45.494
The real weapon in the breaststroke was the legs—and Jack's were strong.

70
00:04:46.514 --> 00:04:51.836
He bent them, bringing his heels up before pushing his legs out and to the sides in powerful

71
00:04:51.896 --> 00:04:58.594
kicks. An instant later Jack returned to the streamlined position.

72
00:04:59.594 --> 00:05:01.575
Then he started all the motions again.

73
00:05:02.496 --> 00:05:06.678
Jack got to the far end of the pool quickly, setting a good pace for the turn.

74
00:05:07.399 --> 00:05:10.920
He palmed the wall, pivoted, kicked off, and took off.

75
00:05:11.401 --> 00:05:18.284
Fantastic! He powered back to the other end of the pool and touched the wall.

76
00:05:18.945 --> 00:05:22.006
Phew! His leg of the race was over!

77
00:05:23.247 --> 00:05:26.433
As his teammate started the butterfly, Jack got out of the pool.

78
00:05:26.453 --> 00:05:29.695
"Good job, Jack!

79
00:05:29.975 --> 00:05:31.956
You got us from fifth place to third!"

80
00:05:32.336 --> 00:05:33.297
Sebastian cried.

81
00:05:35.158 --> 00:05:37.680
Jack nodded, but he was focused on the water.

82
00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.302
Laura was swimming the butterfly, the only girl competing in this relay.

83
00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:45.704
He felt so lucky to have her on his team.

84
00:05:46.605 --> 00:05:47.646
She wasn't just pretty.

85
00:05:48.186 --> 00:05:51.268
She was speedy, smoothly cutting through the water.

86
00:05:54.084 --> 00:05:56.966
She finished fast enough to get the team into second place.

87
00:05:57.926 --> 00:05:59.387
Their anchor was Hulk.

88
00:06:00.007 --> 00:06:06.251
His freestyle was not a pretty sight, unless you liked watching a gigantic machine tearing through the water

89
00:06:06.291 --> 00:06:07.192
like a chainsaw.

90
00:06:08.072 --> 00:06:09.393
But he got the job done.

91
00:06:09.913 --> 00:06:14.376
By the time he reached the turn, he was even with the fastest Pacific Piranhas swimmer.

92
00:06:15.356 --> 00:06:16.817
After the turn he was ahead.

93
00:06:19.338 --> 00:06:24.925
Before he even hit the wall to finish the race, Jack and Sebastian and Laura were jumping up

94
00:06:24.965 --> 00:06:25.405
and down.

95
00:06:28.026 --> 00:06:29.566
They'd won the relay!

96
00:06:31.447 --> 00:06:34.908
Once he'd finished his leg, Hulk tried to hug his teammates.

97
00:06:35.848 --> 00:06:38.849
Jack still had a slight bruise from the last time Hulk had hugged him.

98
00:06:39.509 --> 00:06:42.670
So he backed away, faking an urgent need for the bathroom.

99
00:06:44.151 --> 00:06:47.552
The rest of the meet wasn't as exciting for Jack as the relay race.

100
00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.063
He watched Hulk win the two-hundred-meter freestyle and individual medley races.

101
00:06:54.084 --> 00:06:59.147
He rooted for Laura as she won the girls' butterfly and came in third for the girls' backstroke.

102
00:06:59.988 --> 00:07:05.271
Jack got fifth place in the hundred-meter freestyle and third place in the hundred-meter breaststroke.

103
00:07:06.732 --> 00:07:10.074
Noah had told him he shouldn't complain about not being the best on the team.

104
00:07:10.895 --> 00:07:15.198
And Jack's father had said that being around fast swimmers would help him go faster.

105
00:07:15.978 --> 00:07:18.260
Still, Jack really liked to win.

106
00:07:18.984 --> 00:07:20.866
So he couldn't help feeling disappointed.

107
00:07:22.027 --> 00:07:23.968
The end of the meet was exciting though.

108
00:07:24.749 --> 00:07:26.390
That was when the winner was announced.

109
00:07:27.111 --> 00:07:30.714
The Sharks had beaten the Pacific Piranhas by two points.

110
00:07:30.734 --> 00:07:34.217
"Woo-hoo!" the Sharks cheered.

111
00:07:35.098 --> 00:07:36.199
Jack nudged Laura.

112
00:07:36.219 --> 00:07:40.022
"Is Coach Shin actually smiling?"

113
00:07:40.042 --> 00:07:43.985
"Hmm." Laura peered at their coach, grinning.

114
00:07:44.005 --> 00:07:47.288
"I think so, but it's definitely hard to tell."

115
00:07:48.288 --> 00:07:49.649
"Yay, Jack!"

116
00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:52.991
Luke screamed from where he was sitting with the boys' parents.

117
00:07:53.011 --> 00:07:56.293
"I'm so happy we won!"

118
00:07:56.714 --> 00:07:57.674
Laura exclaimed.

119
00:07:58.855 --> 00:08:01.717
They hugged—until a growl pulled them apart.

120
00:08:03.098 --> 00:08:04.939
"Laura and Jack," Mrs.

121
00:08:04.979 --> 00:08:10.403
Wilson snapped, "the pool deck is no place for a public display of affection!"

122
00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:13.365
Jack shook his head, laughing.

123
00:08:13.385 --> 00:08:16.207
"Thanks, Mrs.

124
00:08:16.247 --> 00:08:19.069
Wilson," he called, giving her a big wave.

125
00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:28.256
Hulk's precious grammy was difficult, but he was starting to get used to her—and everything else in California.
